From 8fa18e8ceb885fd791ed83bbffec9a8266360eba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:12:57 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Controls: swap the shoulders and the triggers

A gamepad's shoulders always pressed the PSP's L and R, and the triggers
their copies or a port's extra buttons, with no way to change it. A
player who wanted L and R on the triggers could not.

The Controls page now has Swap shoulders and triggers
(input.swap_triggers, <prefix>_SWAP_TRIGGERS). On, LT/RT (L2/R2) press
what LB/RB pressed and LB/RB what the triggers pressed: L and R move to
the triggers, and the extra buttons L2 and R2 or a trigger profile's
buttons move to the shoulders. It applies to every gamepad, player 2's
too; the keyboard keeps its own bindings. Restore control defaults turns
it off. The connect line in the log says so.

input::ButtonPrompts::l_r_on_triggers carries it to a profile that draws
the game's button symbols (button_prompts() takes the setting; never in
the PSP style), so a change drops the cached textures and the symbols are
drawn again. The input tests cover it.

Tested with Dissidia 012 on Windows (clang build, USA disc): a scripted
Quick Battle with the swap on and the pad traced (the left trigger sent
L, with circle L + circle; the right trigger R; LB and RB only the extra
buttons L2 and R2), the same run with it off, the row turned on with a
gamepad in the menu and saved, and the game's L/R symbols drawn as the
triggers. Not verified: a real controller, Linux, the Steam Deck,
another game.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
